PS+=['We’re still waiting,\nWaiting for the gifts from above.\nWe wait and wait,\nBut nothing comes.\nGrass and flowers are so down;\nThey can no longer hold their heads up high.\nTrees have nothing to nourish (滋養) their green hair;\nTheir hair turned brown and fell to the ground.\n\nWe’re still waiting,\nWaiting for the gifts from above.\nWe wait and wait,\nBut nothing comes.\nLand and fields (田地) are so sad;\nThey aged so much, with lines all over their faces.\nLakes and ponds gave up the hope long ago;\nThey left for good and will come home no more.\n\nWe’re still waiting,\nWaiting for the gifts from above.\nWe wait and wait,\nBut nothing comes.\nBaby cattle (牛隻) are thirsty for milk,\nBut with no water or pastures (牧草地),\nMother cows give no milk.\nYoung children are crying for rice,\nBut with dry fields and with the ponds shy,\nThe farmers grow no rice.\n\nWe’re still waiting,\nWaiting for the gifts from above.\nWe wait and wait,\nBut nothing comes.',
'【The Baseball Team of the Department of Math (The BOM)・Public Group・150 People】\nCharles Lee　July 11 at 16:15\nAbout the baseball game tomorrow, I have a few important things to say. Tomorrow we’ll be fighting against (對抗) the baseball team of the Department of History. However, the Department of History threw us a curveball there—they changed their starting pitcher (投手) from Xavier Lin to Wayne Hsu. Wayne Hsu is very good at curveballs. Some of you might not know his curveballs well. When he throws a curveball, the ball doesn’t fly straight from beginning to end. It moves down and flies close to the ground before it flies into the catcher’s glove.\nTo deal with this problem, I have to change the batting order tomorrow. The best hitter of our team, Ethan, will be the fourth hitter tomorrow, with Joshua right before him and Jamie batting right after him. The first hitter will be Hank, and the second will be Nelson. The sixth hitter will be Brad, and the hitters following Brad in order will be Steve, Ian, and me. I’m also changing our starting pitcher from Brad to Jamie, for Jamie is in a better state (狀態). Brad will be the catcher tomorrow. The rest of the players will be at the same fielding positions (守備位置) as I told you yesterday. I hope the new batting order will help us face their new starting pitcher and win the game.\nThe baseball game begins at nine o’clock tomorrow morning. Please get to the baseball field (球場) two hours before the game starts, and don’t forget to bring your own water.']
