(25,'Sarah wrote back to Zoe after she read the letter. Which of the following is most likely (可能地) part of the letter?',['...I was so worried because it was difficult to find a place to stay in only a week. When you said I could stay in your apartment, I was so happy and couldn’t thank you enough. Thank you for sending me the floor plan too. Your apartment looks great, and I can’t wait to stay there with you...','...You really need to talk to both of them. First, Karen also uses the bathroom, so she needs to clean it. Although she’s busy, being busy can’t always be an excuse. As for Leo, he needs to clean the kitchen after he uses it. It’s just not right for you to clean every corner of the apartment...','...To be honest, I don’t think changing rooms is a good idea. It’s hard for you to bring this up to them, and it takes you time to move everything to another room. Try to talk to Karen first. Maybe she can make food without that much smoke, for example, chicken soup or salad...','...There are always problems coming up when you share an apartment with someone else. You can try to deal with them or just run away. Don’t give yourself a hard time. If you really don’t feel comfortable about paying the 500 more NT dollars, moving out may be a better idea for you...'],[],3),
