PS+=['Sleeping sickness first appeared in Africa thousands of years ago. People with sleeping sickness have trouble sleeping at night, so they are tired all the time and always feel like dreaming during the day. When a case of sleeping sickness appears in one place, soon many other people living in the same place will get it, too. At first, people thought it had something to do with dark magic. Later, they found out sleeping sickness is caused by (因……而起) several kinds of insects and the parasites (寄生蟲) inside their bodies.\nOne common kind of these insects is the tsetse fly. Tsetse flies feed on the blood (血液) of people and animals like cows and horses. When “they” are biting people, the parasites get into people’s bodies. They would later get to other body parts with blood and give people a headache and a high fever. About a month later, the parasites would get to people’s brains (腦部). With these parasites attacking their brains, people aren’t able to tell days from nights or tell nights from days. The 24-hour sleep-wake cycle (週期) in their brains breaks down, so they can’t fall asleep (睡著的) at night and are too tired to go to work during the day. People might die in months if they don’t take medicine to get the parasites out of their bodies.\nSome people in Africa use nets to catch tsetse flies, and some cover their bodies with clothes to avoid (避免) insect bites. However, there are still thousands of cases of sleeping sickness in Africa every year.']
